/HEAD/LICENSE"},"data":null,"document":null,"weights":null},"links":[{"rel":"primary","url":"https://github.com/777genius/os-ai-computer-use"}],"name":"OS AI Computer Use","notes":"Provider adapters call the OpenAI Responses API with its computer tool (batched actions) or Anthropic's computer-use tool (single actions with zoom); packages/core/src/os_ai_core/tools/computer.py captures the screen and executes actions through per-OS driver ports. macOS uses PyAutoGUI with a Quartz event path for Enter and an AppKit overlay; Windows and Linux (X11 or XWayland) use PyAutoGUI. A Flutter client (macOS, Windows, Linux, web) talks to a local backend; the CLI runs tasks directly. The README headline of 75.0% on OSWorld is a model-provider figure. The repository was formerly iliyaZelenko/os-ai-computer-use (same GitHub repository ID).","published_at":null,"relations":[],"review_status":"curated","scope":"core","summary":"Local desktop agent that sends plain screenshots to OpenAI's or Anthropic's computer-use tool and performs the returned clicks, drags, scrolls and keystrokes through PyAutoGUI-based drivers on macOS, Windows and Linux.","topics":["automation","cross-app"],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://github.com/777genius/os-ai-computer-use"}
